    "https://careers.mtsu.edu/jobs/specialist-sports-programs-murfreesboro-tennessee-tennessee-united-states": {
      "title": "Specialist - Sports Programs",
      "description": "Specialist - Sports Programs - Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Specialist - Sports Programs - Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Kiosk mode Specialist - Sports Programs 498710 Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Recreation Administrative Add to favorites View favorites Job Title Specialist - Sports Programs Department Student Recreation Center Salary $48,920 - $60,252; commensurate with experience Job Summary/Basic Function Reporting to the Assistant Director of Sports Programs, the Coordinator of Sports Programs supports the ongoing development of the Intramural and Club Sports programs while also serving collaboratively in the department of Campus Recreation. The incumbent will focus on the student experience in each respective area of Intramural and Club Sports programs and will work collaboratively with the Assistant Director of Sports Programs to facilitate exceptional experiences that intently serve all MTSU students. The Coordinator of Sports programs will lead various aspects of competitive and non-competitive sports activities with a focus on student engagement and contributing to overall student success and wellbeing. Required Education Bachelor's degree in Recreation, Sports Management or related field required. Required Related Experience No experience required Required License/Registration/Certification CPR certification required Desirable Related Experience One year full time experience in a University Campus Recreation Sports Club Program preferred. Master's degree preferred. Desirable License/Registration/Certification American Red Cross CPR/First Aid/AED instructor required or the ability to obtain instructor certification within the first six months of being hired. Must have valid Tennessee driver's license or the ability to obtain a TN driver's license within one month of being hired. Documents Needed to Apply Cover Letter & Resume Required MTSU offers a comprehensive benefits package, including but not limited to the following: Sick Leave Vacation Leave for Administrative/Classified Staff/12-month Faculty 13 paid University holidays Medical, dental, vision, and life insurance Retirement plans Optional 401K and 403B Deferred Compensation Plans Educational benefits for the employee and their spouse and dependents Click here for additional information. MTSU is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. Proof of U.S. citizenship or eligibility for U.S. employment is required before employment (Immigration Control Act of 1986). Clery Act crime statistics for MTSU are available at https://police.mtsu.edu/annual-security-report/ or by contacting MTSU Public Safety at (615) 898-2424. MTSU is a Tobacco & Drug-Free campus. This position requires a criminal background check. Therefore, you will be required to provide information about your criminal history to be considered. For individuals requiring reasonable accommodation to apply: In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation to apply for a position with MTSU, please call 615-898-2929 or email hrs@mtsu.edu. Application Review Date: October 20, 2026 Back to search results Apply Now First Name (required) 8e4d012c Last Name (required) 7f0aaebb Email (required) a746018e Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Administrative Assistant 3 - Tennessee Livestock Center Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Administrative/Clerical Support, Other Responsible for all department office work, including but not limited to, budget reconciliation and revisions; composition of all correspondence and memorandum, payment authorizations, purchase orders, and payroll paperwork; preparation of legal contracts and department statements; completion of department timesheets; answering telephone and greeting visitors. Associate Athletic Trainer Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Athletics and Coaching The Associate Athletic Trainer will report to the Associate Athletic Director of Sports Medicine. The position will supervise and coordinate athletic training services for student-athletes in intercollegiate athletic programs – primarily men’s basketball. Essential duties include but are not be limited to: assist with the prevention, treatment, rehabilitation, physician referral, and medical documentation of all injuries associated with assigned student athletes; communicate with coaches, student athletes, parents, staff and physicians within NATA and HIPAA guidelines; observe all athletic policy and procedures in accordance with NATA regulations as well as NCAA, Conference USA and MTSU rules and remain certified to perform these duties on a daily basis. Coordinate Concussion testing and baseline testing for all assigned student athletes; provide supervision of daily practice and game coverage, in season travel, and summer sports workout coverage for assigned student athletes as permitted by NCAA legislation. Required to be flexible and adapt to schedule changes as necessary. Serve as an approved preceptor within the CAATE accredited graduate athletic training program. Provide direct supervision of intern athletic trainers for assigned sports and graduate athletic training students in the athletic training education program; instruct these students in professional prevention, care and rehabilitation of assigned student-athletes as well as the certification and licensure process. Required to attend national NATA and Conference USA meetings and/or conventions to remain current in their field for changes that occur. Assistant Director - Event Operations Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Athletics and Coaching, Event Coordination Under the direction of the Associate Athletic Director for Capital Projects, assist in the planning, coordination, and execution of home athletic events across MTSU's 17 NCAA Division I sports and support daily operations of Athletics facilities. Serve as the primary on-site event manager for assigned sports and events; coordinate logistics with visiting teams, game officials, Athletics units, campus departments, contracted vendors, and public safety; support special events and external facility use; assist with operational planning for Athletics capital projects, including the renovation of Floyd Stadium; maintain Athletics inventory records; and assist with hiring, training, and supervising graduate assistants, student workers, and event staff. Night, weekend, and holiday work is required. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert fbe44a80 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Recreation Recreation Employment Type Administrative Administrative Locations Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States First Name (required) 3d2c19ad Last Name (required) 9cdc6987 Email (required) fc922555 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
